From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:08:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(llama-cpp): a switch that refuses a SYCL pool commit, to
 test the refusal on a real device

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch), after the pool's refusal and
the parking prototype.

"A device-memory refusal during a request fails that request, not the
backend" could not be shown by filling the card: at 31,701 of 32,002 MiB,
with three other models loaded, every request was served - the driver pages
an idle neighbour out before it refuses. GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE=N in a
model's environment refuses the next N commits that grow a pool with the
exception a full device raises, so the whole path after it runs on the real
device: the request answered with an error, the backend's process alive,
the next request served. A pool's first commit is never refused: the model
loads. Unset, nothing changes.

STAGED, for a test engine. Compiles (icpx 2025.3.3); not run where it was
written.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 .../0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch        | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..421d690
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0016-sycl-pool-refuse-switch.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+sycl: GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE - a refused pool commit, on demand, for its test
+
+The refusal of a pool commit (the patch before the parking one) fails the
+graph instead of the process. Its test needs a device that refuses, and a
+card cannot be made to on demand: filled to 31,701 of 32,002 MiB (an Intel
+Arc Pro B70, three other models loaded) every request was still served -
+the driver paged an idle neighbour out rather than refuse.
+
+GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE=N refuses the next N commits that GROW a pool: a
+sycl::exception with errc::memory_allocation is raised where the device's
+own would be, so everything after it is the path under test - the pool's
+translation, the unwinding of the temporaries in the middle of a graph, the
+queue drained, GGML_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED, the request's error, the process
+alive and the next request served. A pool's first commit is never refused,
+so the model loads and warms up. Unset, nothing changes; set, the start-up
+log says so as a warning.
+
+Compiles with icpx 2025.3.3; not run where it was written (no device).
+---
+diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+index 720db24..a9599ca 100644
+--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
++++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_vmm = 1;
+ // mapped into a reserved virtual range, GGML_SYCL_PARK_VERIFY=1 reads each unparked buffer back and compares it
+ int g_ggml_sycl_parkable = 0;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_park_verify = 0;
++// for the TEST of a refused pool commit, which a card cannot be made to give on demand (its driver pages an idle
++// neighbour out first): GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE=N refuses the next N commits that GROW a pool, as a full device does
++std::atomic<int> g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse{0};
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_fusion = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_enable_esimd = 1;
+ int g_ggml_sycl_mmvq_wide = 1;
+@@ -450,6 +453,7 @@ static void ggml_check_sycl() try {
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_vmm = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_VMM", 1);
+         g_ggml_sycl_parkable = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_PARKABLE", 0);
+         g_ggml_sycl_park_verify = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_PARK_VERIFY", 0);
++        g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE", 0);
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_fusion = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_FUSION", 1);
+         g_ggml_sycl_enable_esimd = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_ESIMD", 1);
+         g_ggml_sycl_mmvq_wide = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_MMVQ_WIDE", 1);
+@@ -600,6 +604,10 @@ static void ggml_check_sycl() try {
+ #endif
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_PARKABLE: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_parkable);
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_PARK_VERIFY: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_park_verify);
++        if (g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse > 0) {
++            GGML_LOG_WARN("  GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE: %d - the next commits that grow a pool are REFUSED, for a test\n",
++                          g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse.load());
++        }
+ 
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_FUSION: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_enable_fusion);
+         GGML_LOG_INFO("  GGML_SYCL_UPLOAD_STAGING_SLOTS: %d\n", g_ggml_sycl_upload_staging_slots);
+@@ -2465,6 +2473,12 @@ struct ggml_sycl_pool_vmm : public ggml_sycl_pool {
+             // allocate more physical memory
+             std::optional<sycl::ext::oneapi::experimental::physical_mem> phys;
+             try {
++                // the test's refusal: only where a pool GROWS (a load's first commit is left alone, so the model loads),
++                // and raised as the device raises its own, so that everything after this line is the path under test
++                if (pool_size > 0 && g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse > 0 && g_ggml_sycl_pool_refuse.fetch_sub(1) > 0) {
++                    throw sycl::exception(sycl::make_error_code(sycl::errc::memory_allocation),
++                                          "GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE: refused for the test, the device was not asked");
++                }
+                 phys.emplace(dev, ctx, reserve_size);
+             } catch (const sycl::exception & e) {
+                 // nothing of the pool has changed yet: this graph fails, and a later one may ask again
-- 
